{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398474-help-for-creating-high-essence-pc-essence-3-5","id":1398474,"title":"Help for creating high essence PC(Essence 3-5)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-23T17:54:54-07:00","id":1398474,"title":"Help for creating high essence PC(Essence 3-5)","content":"What would be a good number or Exp/Splat Exp to give the players when you want to start a high level game for the different exalts(Solar, DB, Lunar)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:18:36-07:00","id":1398485,"title":"","content":"Is there something wrong with just using the amount of xp that it would take to get there? Like for an Essence 3 Solar give them 125xp and either 75 or 100 Solar xp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T18:55:28-07:00","id":1398498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398474-help-for-creating-high-essence-pc-essence-3-5?p=1398485#post1398485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there something wrong with just using the amount of xp that it would take to get there? Like for an Essence 3 Solar give them 125xp and either 75 or 100 Solar xp?</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with that in nWoD and CoF was that the recomended exp was BS. Is it not like that in Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T19:05:40-07:00","id":1398499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398474-help-for-creating-high-essence-pc-essence-3-5?p=1398498#post1398498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My experience with that in nWoD and CoF was that the recomended exp was BS. Is it not like that in Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>BS as in way too high or way too low? Either way from what I've seen from taking PCs through the game it seems to be okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T19:10:22-07:00","id":1398500,"title":"","content":"Give them the amount needed to get there (maybe a little more so that they can spend all the Normal XP on Charms and still spend enough to be that Essence), divide it by 5, multiply the result by 4, and give that much in Splat XP as well, is how I've done it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T19:43:39-07:00","id":1398506,"title":"","content":"One thing to note is that &quot;the minimum xp to reach a given essence level&quot; will, in natural play, not lead to you having any charms of your new essence. There probably aren't any major problems if you ignore this, but it might make sense to either say &quot;You start at essence 3, with 125 xp worth of essence 1 and 2 charms&quot;, or to start somewhere in the middle of essence 3, at say 175xp.<br /> As for solar/type xp, divide by 5 multiply by 4 is how I usually do it, but that will lead to slightly more solar xp than natural play, depending on how generous the storyteller is/effective the players are at earning type xp. You might want to drop it to a 5:3 ratio or something else between 5:4 and 5:0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T19:49:36-07:00","id":1398508,"title":"","content":"Vance has mentioned nothing breaks if you just give 4 Splat XP to all characters after every session, so 5:4 is perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T03:08:14-07:00","id":1398571,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So how I would go about giving xp for a high powered game will vary depending on how much experience the players have with exalted. If they all know exalted pretty well you can just give them a chunk of XP (I recommend 30-50 XP over the minimum for the Essence rating you want them at so they can have a few charms of that level.) Then they build their character, keeping in mind what essence rating they would be given how much XP they have spent so far.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That could be a bit confusing for newer players who are not used to how spending XP raising essence works, especially if starting off at something other than what the rules assume. In this case I would say: Have X charms of each essence rating (ou can choose a lower rating if desired) as well as some splat Xp that can\u2019t be spent on charms.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Essence 4 Solars: (for essence 3 remove the 1-4 charms and half the 1-3 charms)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7 Essence 1 charms [or Supernal]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">9 Essence 1-2 charms [or Supernal]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">9 Essence 1-3 charms [or supernal]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 Essence 1-4 charms [or supernal]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And 240 Solar XP (160 for Essence 3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Essence 4 Dragon Bloods: (For essence 3 remove the 1-4 charms and 8 or so 1-3 charms)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10 Essence 1-2 charms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">22 Essence 1-3 charms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 Essence 1-4 charms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And 150 Dragon XP (80 of so for Essence 3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t have lunars so I don\u2019t know the break-down for them. This method will result in roughly the same number of charms as you would have by spending all the xp, but is easier to grasp if all of exalted is being thrown at a new player. High essence Exalted can be a ton of fun, but all those possibilities can be smothering for a newer player, so if you can simplify chargen it will be good.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T05:50:55-07:00","id":1398586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398474-help-for-creating-high-essence-pc-essence-3-5?p=1398499#post1398499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BS as in way too high or way too low? Either way from what I've seen from taking PCs through the game it seems to be okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>In vampire requiem 2e they portray a thousand year old vampire having 100 xp if that's the level you're playing. Maybe it's 120, but either way it's too little. As for Ex3, the xp rquirements for certain essence work fine. Just be sure to give the appropriate amonut of bonus xp. Alistair's numbers should be fine. Trust me, your characters will feel appropriately powerful. Unlike longtooth the vampire methuselah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T05:56:56-07:00","id":1398588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398474-help-for-creating-high-essence-pc-essence-3-5?p=1398571#post1398571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#000000][FONT=Arial]S<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t have lunars so I don\u2019t know the break-down for them. This method will result in roughly the same number of charms as you would have by spending all the xp, but is easier to grasp if all of exalted is being thrown at a new player. High essence Exalted can be a ton of fun, but all those possibilities can be smothering for a newer player, so if you can simplify chargen it will be good.</span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree with that method of [x charms at essence 1-y] is a good way of framing it.<br /> It looks like the charm numbers use assume you're halfway between reaching your current essence and the next essence, but the solar xp numbers assume you're about to reach the next essence. Was that intentional? It might be helpful to over-estimate the amount of solar xp, and then say that starting with story merits costs solar xp, since I'd expect most essence 3+ solars to have gained a decent amount of story merits over the course of their lives.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the same amount of xp needed for each essence rating as solars, so the same formula should work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T07:12:56-07:00","id":1398597,"title":"","content":"If you don't have enough Exalted ST experience to know how much XP to give your characters, then meaning no offense and with the best will in the world, you should start with the pregened Tomb of Dreams Adventure, and see how play feels with characters 75% of a starting character. Then progress to letting your players make their own starting characters and going from there.<br /> <br /> Exalted is absolutely unforgiving on newbie STs. A starting character can throw over a thousand successes on a single roll if they build right. The Difficulty Chart runs from 1 to 5. Starting Solars get world shaking Essence 5 powers in their area of focus. <br /> <br /> I built a social tertiary, starting level character who could shout loud enough to shatter bones.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, and, so what? This is EXALTED!&quot;<br /> <br /> That same social tertiary could reliably (84% of the time) convince Ahlat to betray and destroy Harbourhead, without needing to leverage any additional Intimacies beyond her own Charms. And that was the field she naturally sucked at (she was good at physical actions and murdering folks). On a starting character.<br /> <br /> And you want to throw ~125XP on top of that? And presumably you are going to have more than one player?<br /> <br /> An optimized Essence 3-5 Solar is solo-ing Ahlat.<br /> <br /> You're talking about combat scenes that last all night. Dozens of powers on each PC. Exactly one published Antagonist that can match the Circle.<br /> <br /> A Solar can, at Essence 1, attack 8 times then clash any attack made against them.<br /> <br /> If you have a very specific idea for exactly how powerful you want your PCs to be, then give them that much experience.<br /> <br /> But if you don't know exactly what you are trying to achieve... I don't see this ending well.<br /> <br /> If you want to do it, do it.<br /> <br /> But there's a big difference between Essence 5 and Essence 3. Can you describe the kind of game you want to have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T15:49:10-07:00","id":1398653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398474-help-for-creating-high-essence-pc-essence-3-5?p=1398597#post1398597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>We are planning to do a few things with advanced characters.<br /> One is the ability to reach the high levels of power with shortes chronicals. As it stands no game last long enough for us to reach Solar sorcery, or for our DB to get awsome things like Dragon Vortex Attack or its upgrade from Heirs.<br /> <br /> Then the fact that sometimes we like to start the game from the middle. Like, we already have our empire that rivals the reduced state of the Realm after our drawn out war. And we are playing the last desperate battles, with an added third power that took advantage of the conflict to ascend.<br /> <br /> And last, its an idea we are playing with of a flashback kind of game. Where we have several sheets of the same PC an play our characters at different ages, sometimes going back and forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}